  {% include research-project-video.liquid path="cdm/cdm_realworld_single" caption="Single-contact localization on the real Kinova Gen3." %}
  <p>
    In simulation ablations, historical conditioning reduces M-RMSE from 1.33 cm to 0.62 cm. Surface conditioning reduces the average distance from
    generated points to the robot surface from 0.89 cm to 0.29 cm. These measure different effects and are separate from the real-world localization
    results above.
  </p>
  <p>
    The follow-up project, <a href="{{ '/research/projects/contactflowfilter/' | relative_url }}">ContactFlowFilter</a>, combines a generative
    proposal with particle filtering to estimate forces and reason recursively about changing contacts.
  </p>
</section>
